  "term": "Rana pipiens",
  "definition": "Rana pipiens is a frog used in biological research on optic nerve injury and regrowth. In the supplied source, it is the species in which growth factors were studied for their effects on macrophage activity and regenerating retinal ganglion cell axons after nerve crush.",
